  "reason": "The strongest signal so far is that multiprofile with avgpool aggregation (config_018, acc=0.6186) dramatically outperforms singleprofile (config_016, acc=0.5266), a +9.2% jump. The fusion method (concat vs weighted) showed negligible difference in singleprofile (~0.3%), so that axis is low priority. The key remaining uncertainty within the multiprofile setting is whether the aggregation method matters: does simple average pooling suffice, or can a transformer learn profile-level interactions that further improve performance? config_020 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other variables constant (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat), making it a clean single-variable test that directly extends the best-performing configuration. If transformer aggregation helps, it opens a high-impact architectural direction; if not, we confirm avgpool is sufficient and can redirect budget toward the image encoder (ViT-L) or RNA encoder axes. This is the highest-information next step under the limited budget."
